From 2028cbdc9b7b717a45fb2f55b4b7116e1905f3f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:28:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Added: Add copy and paste to the extra keys and the SFTP
 editor toolbar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The default extra keys have ⧉ (COPY) and ⎘ (PASTE) right of A+ and A-.
⧉ copies the selected text, or tells how to select text if nothing is
selected, and swiping up on it copies the screen. Ctrl+Shift+C copies
the same way.

The SFTP editor toolbar has cut, copy, paste and select all after undo
and redo. Cut and copy take the line of the cursor if nothing is
selected, paste replaces the selection with plain text, and cut and
paste are undone as steps of their own. In the hex view, copy takes the
hex dump of up to the first 64 KB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GLNsTPnn2xKUQ4uFcevT6G
---
